A1 Stitcher is an independent implementation. It is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Antigravity or Insta360. Camera names identify compatible formats.

The Insta360 decoder and protobuf schema in AdrianEddy/telemetry-parser informed
interpretation of the indexed trailer and metadata field numbers:
https://github.com/AdrianEddy/telemetry-parser
Reference revision: d45ebf2afce85fa691838fd32b3da8ae2fcac773 (MIT / Apache-2.0).
No telemetry-parser code or runtime dependency is distributed in this package.

The 0.4.0 GPS decoder independently implements the observed 53-byte record-7
layout, also described by telemetry-parser's insta360/record.rs and ExifTool's
QuickTimeStream.pl (ProcessInsta360):
https://github.com/AdrianEddy/telemetry-parser/blob/d45ebf2afce85fa691838fd32b3da8ae2fcac773/src/insta360/record.rs
https://github.com/exiftool/exiftool/blob/master/lib/Image/ExifTool/QuickTimeStream.pl
No ExifTool code is copied, distributed or required at runtime. GPX output follows:
https://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/

BenjaminHenriksson/insv-stitch provided a useful public MEI/X5 pipeline reference:
https://github.com/BenjaminHenriksson/insv-stitch
Reference revision: 722b9c7915fc372cdeb73ca25c931cec00f36e13 (MIT).
The A1 lens mapping and measured attitude convention are implemented separately;
X5-specific constants and its per-unit IMU transform are not A1 defaults.

Spherical Video V2 box layouts follow Google's public specification:
https://github.com/google/spatial-media/blob/master/docs/spherical-video-v2-rfc.md

NumPy, SciPy and OpenCV are separately installed dependencies with their own
licenses. FFmpeg is a separately installed executable; the package neither
bundles it nor changes the licensing of a user's chosen FFmpeg build.

The 0.2.0 overlap estimator uses OpenCV's separately installed DIS optical flow:
https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/de/d4f/classcv_1_1DISOpticalFlow.html
Read-only inspection of the user's Studio installation exposed feature names
for optical-flow stitching, image fusion, intensity-ratio maps and gyro filtering.
Those observations informed hypotheses; no Studio code, shaders, model weights,
libraries or internal parameter tables are included or invoked by this project.

The 0.3.0 periodic seam search is an independently authored dynamic program.
Additional read-only Studio feature/symbol inspection exposed seam-finder and
propeller-guard capability names; these are clues, not evidence of identical
algorithms. No vendor masks or learned models are distributed or used.

The 0.7.0 exposure midpoint clock and native visibility masks are independently
authored. Read-only inspection of Studio timing/visibility interfaces and metadata
field-number constants informed format hypotheses. The implementation does not
load vendor libraries, copy vendor algorithms or distribute per-camera masks.
See docs/quality-v0.7.md for observations, official guide links and measured limits.

The 0.8 image-to-trajectory timing fitter, camera-fixed obstruction proposals,
continuous comparison tool and three-band overlap blend are independently authored.
Public references considered for the problem and terminology:
https://github.com/gyroflow/rs-sync (LGPL-2.1; no code or dependency copied)
https://docs.opencv.org/4.13.0/d5/d4b/classcv_1_1detail_1_1MultiBandBlender.html
No rs-sync implementation, Studio code, vendor masks or model weights are bundled.
The multiband mode uses an independent bounded-belt frequency decomposition, not
OpenCV's whole-panorama MultiBandBlender class.
